# ─── Frontend ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
NEXT_PUBLIC_REALTIME_URL=http://localhost:8086
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=ws://localhost:8086

# Override the docs site base URL (default: https://beenuar.github.io/AiSOC/docs).
# Set this when serving docs from a custom domain like https://docs.tryaisoc.com/docs.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DOCS_URL=https://docs.tryaisoc.com/docs

# ─── Service-to-service auth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared bearer token for backend services that are NOT reachable from the
# browser (purple-team, honeytokens, ueba). Those surfaces execute privileged
# work — purple-team can start adversary-emulation operations against live
# hosts — and they fail closed: with no token configured and AISOC_DEV_MODE
# unset, they answer 503 rather than serving the route openly.
#
# Leave blank for local `docker compose up` (AISOC_DEV_MODE covers it). Set a
# real value for anything network-reachable.
#
# `ingest` and `connectors` also use it, and there AISOC_DEV_MODE does NOT
# cover it: POST /v1/ingest is a write into tenant-owned data and has no
# dev-mode shortcut. Set this on both services to let the connector-poll
# path push; a direct curl/script push uses a per-tenant token from
# `make ingest-token` instead and needs nothing here. See
# apps/docs/docs/operations/ingest-authentication.md.
AISOC_SERVICE_TOKEN=
# Optional per-service overrides, if you'd rather not share one secret:
# AISOC_PURPLE_TEAM_SERVICE_TOKEN=
# AISOC_HONEYTOKENS_SERVICE_TOKEN=
# AISOC_UEBA_SERVICE_TOKEN=
# AISOC_INGEST_SERVICE_TOKEN=
